        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "General and associated examination findings via video"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Appeared tired but not acutely unwell, speaking in full sentences, no obvious shortness of breath; pink colour and no cyanosis. Lips and oral mucosa appeared normal when opening mouth; no conjunctival injection."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Other reported symptoms and pertinent negatives"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports fatigue and slightly reduced appetite, but drinking adequately. No reported discharge, vesicles, oral ulcers, eye pain, shortness of breath, chest pain, abdominal pain, diarrhoea, or urinary symptoms."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Forearm skin punch biopsy"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Dense dermal neutrophilic infiltrate with papillary dermal oedema; no leukocytoclastic vasculitis and organisms not seen. Features consistent with acute febrile neutrophilic dermatosis (Sweet syndrome) in the appropriate clinical context."
      }
    },
